<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Resources/Vigil-Dev.entitlements — local development only. NEVER DISTRIBUTED.

    Implements docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §13.4. Selected by the sandbox-off flag of build-app.sh, which
    prints a loud warning and stamps VigilDevBuild=true into the bundle's Info.plist so the About
    window can show it.

    Why it exists: turning the sandbox off removes the provisioning-profile requirement around the
    managed multicast entitlement, which is what unblocks day-to-day SADP work on a laptop that has
    no Apple grant.

    What it does NOT do: unsandboxed is still subject to the macOS 15 local-network prompt, so a
    denied prompt still makes discovery silently find nothing.

    com.apple.security.get-task-allow permits a debugger to attach. It must be absent from anything
    that leaves the build machine; a notarisation submission carrying it is rejected.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>

    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <false/>

    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- The default clip and snapshot destination, ~/Movies/Vigil.
         Without this, `.moviesDirectory` resolves to `Data/Movies` inside the container, which is a
         symlink to the real folder — so `createDirectory` fails with NSCocoaErrorDomain 513
         (NSFileWriteNoPermissionError) and recording refuses to start. Observed on the first real
         recording attempt; the path in the error is what named the cause.
         `files.user-selected.read-write` below does NOT cover this: it grants only what the user
         picks in a panel, and the default destination is never picked. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.assets.movies.read-write</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Debugger attach. Development only. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.get-task-allow</key>
    <true/>

</dict>
</plist>
